<h1 class="page-title" data-page-title-uuid="00000000-0000-88da-b36e-289718ab00fd">AirVisual monitors — ship-air</h1>

2 devices · 81 samples across 20 series, <time datetime="2024-08-30T23:00:00+00:00" title="2024-08-30 23:00:00 UTC">Fri Aug 30th, 2024 at 23:00</time> — <time datetime="2024-11-03T11:45:09+00:00" title="2024-11-03 11:45:09 UTC">Sun Nov 3rd, 2024 at 11:45</time>.

Every value is as the device logged it; the sampling interval follows the device's own sensor-mode schedule, so the markers are unevenly spaced by design.

## Plots

### Particulate matter

PM1, PM2.5 and PM10 mass concentration from the device's laser particle counter. PM1 ⊂ PM2.5 ⊂ PM10, so the three lines nest.

6 series · 216 points · <time datetime="2024-08-30T23:00:00+00:00" title="2024-08-30 23:00:00 UTC">Fri Aug 30th, 2024 at 23:00</time> — <time datetime="2024-11-03T11:45:09+00:00" title="2024-11-03 11:45:09 UTC">Sun Nov 3rd, 2024 at 11:45</time>

<div class="time-series-chart" data-time-series="00000000-0000-804e-809f-21e745e7e90f 00000000-0000-85a7-9500-e94da9507fd6 00000000-0000-81eb-8c79-94d38d9e1384 00000000-0000-8274-84e3-ef525ca4e38c 00000000-0000-8e07-86b1-15565691a55e 00000000-0000-833e-857e-a59ba3f51467"></div>

### Air quality index

The device's own PM2.5 index on the US and Chinese scales, and the index of the outdoor station it follows. An index, not a concentration: 0–50 is good on the US scale.

8 series · 290 points · <time datetime="2024-08-30T23:00:00+00:00" title="2024-08-30 23:00:00 UTC">Fri Aug 30th, 2024 at 23:00</time> — <time datetime="2024-11-03T11:45:09+00:00" title="2024-11-03 11:45:09 UTC">Sun Nov 3rd, 2024 at 11:45</time>

<div class="time-series-chart" data-time-series="00000000-0000-8b31-8532-5391f897ea54 00000000-0000-8588-97cc-0acf8df8de20 00000000-0000-8c55-858e-67e412aa2a48 00000000-0000-8cc8-b5cc-3a86275e0eeb 00000000-0000-8a43-b381-4465c5be8afb 00000000-0000-8bf4-8b69-96b4ebb917ee 00000000-0000-832f-987a-bbafb03ad562 00000000-0000-8560-9726-6a1d8f897e31"></div>

### CO₂

Carbon dioxide. Outdoor air is ~420 ppm; a closed room with people in it climbs past 1000.

2 series · 73 points · <time datetime="2024-08-30T23:00:00+00:00" title="2024-08-30 23:00:00 UTC">Fri Aug 30th, 2024 at 23:00</time> — <time datetime="2024-11-03T11:45:09+00:00" title="2024-11-03 11:45:09 UTC">Sun Nov 3rd, 2024 at 11:45</time>

<div class="time-series-chart" data-time-series="00000000-0000-8118-8d0e-77e2d5415d6e 00000000-0000-828a-82c4-595bcc35fcb2"></div>

### Temperature

Degrees Celsius. The device also logs Fahrenheit; that column is kept in the sample payload and not plotted twice.

2 series · 73 points · <time datetime="2024-08-30T23:00:00+00:00" title="2024-08-30 23:00:00 UTC">Fri Aug 30th, 2024 at 23:00</time> — <time datetime="2024-11-03T11:45:09+00:00" title="2024-11-03 11:45:09 UTC">Sun Nov 3rd, 2024 at 11:45</time>

<div class="time-series-chart" data-time-series="00000000-0000-858c-a215-ec292186737f 00000000-0000-8d3d-bd55-9b3c023fe814"></div>

### Relative humidity

Relative humidity is already a dimensionless ratio — no conversion applies.

2 series · 69 points · <time datetime="2024-08-30T23:00:00+00:00" title="2024-08-30 23:00:00 UTC">Fri Aug 30th, 2024 at 23:00</time> — <time datetime="2024-11-03T11:45:09+00:00" title="2024-11-03 11:45:09 UTC">Sun Nov 3rd, 2024 at 11:45</time>

<div class="time-series-chart" data-time-series="00000000-0000-8d1e-a54d-622256434f83 00000000-0000-8ea0-a9fb-bd4b5ff9595f"></div>

